# UI Design — Professional Portfolio

Visual goal: **credible senior developer** — calm, readable, recruiter-friendly. Not a creative agency showcase.

## Design Principles

- **Speed over decoration** — if an effect costs LCP or JS, cut it (see `performance.mdc`)
- **Clarity over decoration** — content (projects, experience) is the hero
- **Consistent rhythm** — uniform section padding, heading sizes, card gaps
- **Restrained motion** — subtle hover/focus only; no scroll-jacking or particle backgrounds
- **Both themes polished** — light default; dark mode equally intentional

## Hero

- **Typography-first** — name, title, CTAs render as HTML without hero image (best LCP)
- Optional avatar: small, circular, `priority` only if ≤ 80 KB and explicit width/height
- No full-bleed background photos or video on home
- CTAs: plain buttons/links — no animated gradients

## Color System

Use CSS variables in `globals.css` — ShadCN-compatible tokens.

| Role | Light | Dark |
|------|-------|------|
| Background | near-white (`zinc-50`) | near-black (`zinc-950`) |
| Foreground | `zinc-900` | `zinc-50` |
| Muted text | `zinc-600` | `zinc-400` |
| Accent | single accent — e.g. `blue-600` / `sky-500` | slightly brighter for contrast |
| Border | `zinc-200` | `zinc-800` |

- **One accent color** for links, primary buttons, focus rings
- No rainbow gradients on hero; optional subtle gradient on hero background is OK if low contrast
- Skill tags: muted badges — not neon

## Typography Scale

| Element | Class guidance |
|---------|----------------|
| Hero name | `text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight` |
| Section title | `text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold` |
| Body | `text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground` |
| Small meta | `text-sm text-muted-foreground` |

- Max line length for prose: `max-w-prose` (~65ch)
- Code in blog: monospace, slightly smaller, bordered surface

## Layout

- **Header:** sticky, blurred backdrop, logo/name + nav + locale + theme toggle
- **Footer:** copyright, social icons (LinkedIn, Telegram, GitHub if added), minimal links
- **Home flow:** Hero → Highlights/Skills strip → Featured Projects → Experience teaser → Blog teaser → Contact CTA
- **Projects page:** grid `md:grid-cols-2` cards with image, title, summary, stack badges, links
- **About page:** photo optional — professional headshot if provided in `public/`

## Components Look & Feel

### Project Card

- Border card, rounded-lg, hover:border-accent/50
- Stack as small `Badge` components
- Primary action: "View case study" internal; "Visit site" external with icon

### Experience Timeline

- Vertical timeline with year + role + company
- Muted connector line; no heavy illustration

### Skills

- Grouped categories with icon optional (lucide, single stroke)
- "Learning" group visually distinct (dashed border or muted label) for NestJS

## Dark Mode

- `next-themes` with `class` strategy on `<html>`
- Toggle in header; icons sun/moon with `aria-label`
- Test contrast in both modes — see `accessibility.mdc`
- Images: slight brightness reduction in dark mode optional (`dark:brightness-90`)

## Icons

- **Lucide React** — consistent 1.5px stroke, size 16–20px inline, 24px in buttons
- Social icons in footer only — not scattered

## Responsive

- Mobile nav: hamburger → sheet/drawer; full nav links + locale + theme inside
- Project grid: single column on mobile
- Hero CTAs: stack vertically on small screens

## Do Not

- Glassmorphism overload, 3D transforms, cursor trails
- Stock photo hero backgrounds unrelated to developer identity
- Comic Sans, excessive emoji in professional sections
- Auto-playing carousels for projects

## OG Image

- Static `public/og-image.png` — 1200×630, name + title + subtle brand color
- Regenerate when title or branding changes
